WEBVTT

00:30.322 --> 00:33.951
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:44.044 --> 00:46.879
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION
SOME SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:46.880 --> 00:49.048
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:50.342 --> 00:53.136
THE CRADLE OF ELITE SOLDIERS

00:57.599 --> 00:59.518
- Company, attention!
-  Attention!

01:00.727 --> 01:04.481
I don't care what kind of
people you were outside.

01:05.274 --> 01:09.403
The only thing I'm interested in
is making true soldiers out of you,

01:09.987 --> 01:12.905
so make sure to give it your all
in training. Understood?

01:12.906 --> 01:14.448
Understood, sir!

01:14.449 --> 01:16.535
That was pathetic!
Everyone, down on the ground!

01:17.286 --> 01:19.079
Down on the ground!

01:20.872 --> 01:23.958
On one, "I will."
On two, "Chant louder."

01:23.959 --> 01:25.918
- One!
-  I will!

01:25.919 --> 01:27.003
-  Two!
- Chant louder!

01:27.004 --> 01:28.671
Is that the best you can do?

01:28.672 --> 01:30.464
- One!
-  I will!

01:30.465 --> 01:32.133
- Two!
- Chant louder!

01:32.134 --> 01:33.426
- One!
- I will!

01:33.427 --> 01:34.885
- Two!
- Chant louder!

01:34.886 --> 01:36.512
- One!
- I will!

01:36.513 --> 01:40.266
Korean men have a duty
to serve in the military.

01:40.267 --> 01:41.268
Chant louder!

01:48.191 --> 01:50.609
What do you think
you're doing, putting on makeup?

01:50.610 --> 01:51.987
All troops, on your feet!

01:53.572 --> 01:55.573
To the signpost and back!

01:55.574 --> 01:56.992
Run!

01:58.702 --> 02:00.162
Faster!

02:01.038 --> 02:02.831
Our Creed.

02:04.082 --> 02:06.625
One. We defend liberal democracy

02:06.626 --> 02:08.045
and help reunify the nation.

02:12.758 --> 02:18.304
Two. We train as if in real combat
and become victors in ground warfare.

02:18.305 --> 02:19.306
One!

02:20.307 --> 02:21.308
Two!

02:21.808 --> 02:23.517
Three!

02:23.518 --> 02:24.686
Four!

02:25.354 --> 02:27.189
What the heck?

02:28.899 --> 02:30.691
Sir, it's a rock!

02:30.692 --> 02:33.110
No kidding, you idiot.
Of course it's a rock.

02:33.111 --> 02:36.113
- I think I sprained my back. Help!
-  Come on, be quiet.

02:36.114 --> 02:37.823
- Help!
-  Hey, man. Be quiet!

02:37.824 --> 02:38.908
- Why am I!
-  Two!

02:38.909 --> 02:39.992
Like this?

02:39.993 --> 02:41.577
-  One!
- Why am I!

02:41.578 --> 02:43.079
- Two!
- Like this?

02:43.080 --> 02:44.538
-  One!
- Why am I!

02:44.539 --> 02:46.165
-  Two!
- Like this?

02:46.166 --> 02:48.417
-  We!
- Can do it!

02:48.418 --> 02:50.503
- We!
- Can do it!

02:50.504 --> 02:51.922
- Left foot!
-  Three.

02:52.631 --> 02:54.632
-  Left foot!
-  We obey regulations…

02:54.633 --> 02:56.175
Thirty seconds left to eat!

02:56.176 --> 02:58.010
…and follow the orders of our superiors.

02:58.011 --> 03:00.179
Anyone leaving leftovers
will regret it. Got it?

03:00.180 --> 03:01.264
Yes, sir!

03:07.187 --> 03:09.523
I can…

03:11.024 --> 03:12.275
…do it!

03:12.859 --> 03:15.779
I can…

03:18.907 --> 03:19.908
Sir!

03:20.742 --> 03:22.952
Please… help me!

03:22.953 --> 03:25.622
It'll take more than that
to save our nation!

03:31.711 --> 03:34.923
I can't save it because…

03:36.466 --> 03:37.801
I'm not a soldier.

03:41.179 --> 03:43.139
ASSISTANT INSTRUCTOR

03:43.140 --> 03:46.768
CONFIDENCE WALL
INCLINED WALL SCALING

03:53.150 --> 03:54.316
Oh.

03:57.904 --> 04:00.782
Hey! Don't we have a medic here?

04:03.285 --> 04:04.411
Move!

04:04.995 --> 04:06.121
Hey, push!

04:07.205 --> 04:09.039
Wait! You shouldn't move him like that.

04:09.040 --> 04:10.834
:cue

04:14.588 --> 04:17.131
It's a fracture.
Any orthopedic surgeons?

04:17.132 --> 04:18.758
I'm an orthopedic surgeon.

04:20.427 --> 04:21.802
- Please take a look.
- Okay.

04:21.803 --> 04:24.638
Sir, I'm going to apply pressure here.

04:24.639 --> 04:27.183
- Can you feel anything?
- How's the patient?

04:27.184 --> 04:29.852
No fractures,
but the laceration is deep.

04:29.853 --> 04:32.439
We need to irrigate and suture it
before it gets infected.

04:33.815 --> 04:35.901
Do we have any alcohol
and saline solution?

04:40.489 --> 04:42.698
Don't scrunch your face,
or the wound might open.

04:42.699 --> 04:43.783
Please hang in there.

04:43.784 --> 04:45.826
Hand me the saline solution. Hurry.

04:45.827 --> 04:47.621
Hold down his hands, please.

04:53.585 --> 04:56.797
I'm a public health doctor
who's to serve a three-year term

04:57.547 --> 05:03.135
in medically underserved areas
in lieu of regular military service.

05:03.136 --> 05:05.430
PUBLIC HEALTH DOCTOR

05:07.390 --> 05:09.058
It's a closed fracture in the left arm.

05:09.059 --> 05:10.559
Okay.

05:10.560 --> 05:14.605
- Can you feel anything in your fingertips?
- No, I can't.

05:14.606 --> 05:18.192
Sir, would you mind
if I sutured this laceration?

05:18.193 --> 05:20.487
Uh. Would you do that for me?

05:25.492 --> 05:26.575
Wait.

05:26.576 --> 05:27.577
Yes?

05:28.453 --> 05:30.288
Would this leave a scar on my face?

05:31.164 --> 05:32.749
I'm an aspiring actor.

05:33.542 --> 05:34.793
If I got a scar on my face…

05:35.377 --> 05:37.127
You don't have to worry about that.

05:37.128 --> 05:39.797
He's a board-certified plastic surgeon
at a university hospital.

05:39.798 --> 05:41.298
He'll make sure there's no scar.

05:43.009 --> 05:44.803
- Thank you.
- Sure.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.639
- Please turn your head a little.
- Okay.

07:25.028 --> 07:27.029
Make sure not to get any water on it.

07:27.030 --> 07:30.033
You'll have to get it dressed every day
until the stitches are removed.

07:30.784 --> 07:34.663
To be honest, I used to think
the PH docs were pathetic.

07:35.413 --> 07:38.082
I couldn't help but wonder
how they had become doctors

07:38.083 --> 07:40.167
when they couldn't even
do a drill properly.

07:40.168 --> 07:42.544
Well, we're more accustomed
to studying at a desk, so…

07:42.545 --> 07:44.339
But I was wrong.

07:44.964 --> 07:48.176
The way you ran over to us
without any hesitation…

07:49.594 --> 07:51.303
You were like superheroes.

07:51.304 --> 07:54.640
IT IS OUR DUTY
TO SAVE OUR COMRADES' LIVES

07:54.641 --> 07:55.766
Thank you.

07:55.767 --> 07:57.518
2ND TRAINING BATTALION BARRACKS

07:57.519 --> 07:59.312
Where are you thinking of applying?

08:00.313 --> 08:02.523
Well, it's not like
things would go my way,

08:02.524 --> 08:04.608
since it's all up to the luck of the draw.

08:04.609 --> 08:05.943
I'm fine anywhere but an island.

08:05.944 --> 08:07.654
True. Islands are the worst.

08:08.488 --> 08:11.366
But if you do end up going to one,
be wary of three things.

08:12.784 --> 08:14.993
Three things?

08:14.994 --> 08:16.453
What three things?

08:16.454 --> 08:17.955
It's just something I heard.

08:17.956 --> 08:21.041
They say there are three things
that'll make your life a living hell.

08:21.042 --> 08:24.461
Incidents, people, and love.

08:24.462 --> 08:27.340
And if you get caught up in all three,
you'll never escape.
:cue

08:29.592 --> 08:34.806
Incidents, people, and love?

08:37.851 --> 08:39.727
Trainees!

08:39.728 --> 08:41.353
Which one of you was chatting?

08:41.354 --> 08:43.605
- I'm sorry, sir!
- Why are you dressed like that?

08:43.606 --> 08:44.773
Where's your cap?

08:44.774 --> 08:46.942
My cap? Oh, my cap…

08:46.943 --> 08:48.152
Why, you little!

08:48.153 --> 08:50.780
- Down on the ground!
-  Down on the ground!

08:51.906 --> 08:55.284
On one, "Dress code."
On two, "Violation." One!

08:55.285 --> 08:56.493
Dress code!

08:56.494 --> 08:58.454
- Two!
- Violation!

08:58.455 --> 09:00.622
- One!
- Dress code!

09:00.623 --> 09:02.875
- Two!
- Violation!

09:02.876 --> 09:04.084
- One!
- Dress code!

09:04.085 --> 09:05.086
No way.

09:05.962 --> 09:07.881
There's no way I'd end up on an island.

09:08.590 --> 09:10.759
I couldn't possibly be that unlucky.

09:17.599 --> 09:18.725
I…

09:19.392 --> 09:20.684
was that unlucky.

09:22.145 --> 09:23.604
YEOPOONG MARINE TRANSPORT

09:23.605 --> 09:28.902
EPISODE 1
THE DOCTOR SENT TO THE ISLAND

09:29.527 --> 09:32.072
Wow, for real? Okay.

09:32.739 --> 09:34.741
I guess I should go.

09:37.869 --> 09:39.578
I really don't think I can do this.

09:39.579 --> 09:42.082
Seriously, I really don't think I can go.

09:42.916 --> 09:44.541
You have to go, dumbass.

09:44.542 --> 09:45.919
What else can you do?

09:48.588 --> 09:49.589
Oh, man…

09:58.681 --> 09:59.765
Hey, Gangseok.

09:59.766 --> 10:01.100
Are you leaving now?

10:01.101 --> 10:02.392
Yeah.

10:02.393 --> 10:03.645
You're in for a rough time.

10:04.395 --> 10:06.688
- How about your meds?
- Not yet.

10:06.689 --> 10:09.733
Those meds can cause side effects
like memory loss, dizziness,

10:09.734 --> 10:13.362
and hallucinations,
so not taking them would be ideal.

10:13.363 --> 10:14.364
I know.

10:15.115 --> 10:18.409
You heard the news about Hwayeong, right?

10:20.203 --> 10:23.497
Hey, so things haven't changed
between you guys?

10:23.498 --> 10:25.500
It's been a long time since Seonu left.

10:26.584 --> 10:28.085
So much time has passed…

10:28.086 --> 10:29.546
So what if time has passed?

10:31.005 --> 10:33.383
Scars aren't something
that heal over time.

10:34.134 --> 10:35.260
Scars…

10:37.220 --> 10:38.596
are healed with money.

10:40.473 --> 10:43.268
If you're worried about my scars,
shut your mouth and open your wallet.

10:44.185 --> 10:46.353
-  Hello? Jiui.
- Yeah.

10:46.354 --> 10:48.438
- Good luck out there.
- Thanks, Gangseok.

10:48.439 --> 10:49.440
Sure.

11:17.302 --> 11:21.513
The ship bound for
Pyeondongdo, Pyeondongdo is now departing.

11:21.514 --> 11:23.307
Go. You have to go, you crazy bastard.

11:23.308 --> 11:27.311
All remaining passengers,
please board the ship at this time.

11:29.022 --> 11:33.276
The ship bound for Pyeondongdo,
Pyeondongdo is now departing.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.987
All remaining passengers…

11:55.381 --> 11:56.716
Please…

12:01.054 --> 12:03.223
DO JI UI, M
ELLMARP

12:09.938 --> 12:11.481
Two hours to Pyeondongdo.

12:14.859 --> 12:16.277
All I have to do is fall asleep.

12:17.570 --> 12:18.988
Nothing's going to happen.

12:20.031 --> 12:21.115
Nothing.
:cue

12:55.316 --> 12:56.984
We need to get
our numbers straight.

12:56.985 --> 12:58.402
Excuse me, young man.

12:58.403 --> 12:59.486
Hey, young man.

12:59.487 --> 13:00.989
Hey, open your eyes.

13:01.698 --> 13:03.865
Young man!

13:03.866 --> 13:07.160
There's something we'd like to ask you.

13:07.161 --> 13:09.288
My friend here
didn't have any cash,

13:09.289 --> 13:12.082
so she agreed to pay us back later
and borrowed…

13:15.336 --> 13:17.170
That leaves 3,000 won, right?

13:40.862 --> 13:41.863
That's…

13:42.905 --> 13:44.073
dangerous.

14:08.473 --> 14:09.932
Excuse me.

14:13.519 --> 14:15.021
Excuse me!

14:17.690 --> 14:19.566
That's dangerous. Get down from there now.

14:19.567 --> 14:21.151
Whoa.

14:21.152 --> 14:23.153
Don't step any closer.

14:23.154 --> 14:25.031
Don't do it. Get down from there!

14:45.635 --> 14:46.636
Hey!

14:49.597 --> 14:50.723
No.

15:12.495 --> 15:13.870
Someone's fallen overboard!

15:13.871 --> 15:15.498
Stop the boat!

15:17.625 --> 15:19.669
I said someone's fallen overboard!

16:18.644 --> 16:19.687
:cue

16:36.829 --> 16:40.415
Take three steps outside,
and you'll find fish everywhere.

16:40.416 --> 16:42.751
So why are you looking
at the fish inside a tank?

16:42.752 --> 16:45.713
Come on, these guys
are different from those guys.

16:46.631 --> 16:49.633
They're raised for consumption.
These guys are meant for observing.

16:49.634 --> 16:51.761
They're totally different.

16:52.929 --> 16:55.722
Why are you even ranking fish?

16:55.723 --> 16:58.141
Whether they live
in seawater or tap water,

16:58.142 --> 17:00.018
they all live in water just the same.

17:00.019 --> 17:03.396
Oh, right.
You saw my leave request, right?

17:03.397 --> 17:07.108
Hey, I told you to put in requests
at least three days in advance, didn't I?

17:07.109 --> 17:10.154
I'll take care of it
this time, but don't let it happen again.

17:11.197 --> 17:12.949
Okay. Thank you.

17:15.284 --> 17:16.743
Granny.

17:16.744 --> 17:17.994
- Granny Sunja.
-  Yes?

17:17.995 --> 17:19.746
- Let's have you go inside.
- Okay.

17:19.747 --> 17:21.289
- Is it that room?
- Yes.

17:21.290 --> 17:24.209
I've opened the door,
so all you need to do is step inside.

17:24.210 --> 17:26.836
We haven't heard from
the new doctor yet, have we?

17:26.837 --> 17:28.964
No. They said
the ferry already arrived, though.

17:28.965 --> 17:31.383
Mmm. Must've been a paddle boat.

17:31.384 --> 17:33.885
Think he might have gotten lost?

17:33.886 --> 17:36.137
A smart doctor getting lost?

17:36.138 --> 17:39.224
On this tiny island?

17:39.225 --> 17:41.269
I'm telling you,
he's definitely taken a detour.

17:41.894 --> 17:43.436
Should I try giving him a call?

17:43.437 --> 17:44.438
I'll do it.

17:46.023 --> 17:49.109
I'm going to give him an earful and
really straighten him out.

17:49.110 --> 17:50.569
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

17:58.786 --> 17:59.787
Damn it.

18:05.626 --> 18:07.168
Hello?

18:07.169 --> 18:08.379
Dr. Do Jiui?

18:09.672 --> 18:10.881
Yes, who is this?

18:11.549 --> 18:14.010
I'm calling from
the Pyeondongdo Public Health Center.

18:15.386 --> 18:17.638
What is the Pyeondongdo
Public Health Center?

18:22.101 --> 18:23.686
Dr. Do Jiui?

18:35.406 --> 18:39.159
Goodness, I had no idea
you were already here.

18:39.160 --> 18:41.494
We've been looking all over for you.

18:41.495 --> 18:42.788
Ugh.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.500
What happened?

18:47.501 --> 18:49.127
How about that woman?

18:49.128 --> 18:50.712
Is she still alive?

18:50.713 --> 18:51.922
What is he rambling about?

18:52.423 --> 18:54.842
I guess you must've had
a pretty wild dream.

18:55.885 --> 18:57.177
- A dream?
- Oh, my.

18:57.178 --> 18:59.888
I heard someone passed out on the ferry,

18:59.889 --> 19:02.098
so I thought it might be
a tourist or a fisherman

19:02.099 --> 19:03.767
who had drunk too much.

19:03.768 --> 19:06.812
Never did I guess
it would be our doctor.

19:07.855 --> 19:09.939
Wait, so that was really a dream?

19:09.940 --> 19:13.109
Mmm. That's enough.
It's time for you to wake up.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.778
I'll show you the health center.

19:14.779 --> 19:17.990
You'll be here for a year,
so you should get familiar with the place.

19:19.116 --> 19:20.576
- Right.
- Come on.

19:24.664 --> 19:25.665
Here.

19:26.332 --> 19:29.501
He's coming out right on time.
Please introduce yourselves.

19:29.502 --> 19:32.379
This is Dr. Yong Jucheon
from the Korean Medicine ward.

19:32.380 --> 19:34.507
This here is our new surgeon, Dr. Do Jiui.

19:35.091 --> 19:36.174
Hello.

19:36.175 --> 19:37.550
Ooh!

19:37.551 --> 19:39.344
You were carried in earlier, right?

19:39.345 --> 19:42.347
So you're a doctor
assigned here, huh?

19:42.348 --> 19:43.932
We're really glad to have you.

19:43.933 --> 19:45.433
Hold on.

19:45.434 --> 19:47.019
If you're a doctor, here.

19:47.770 --> 19:50.397
- Sorry?
-  I'm asking for your number.

19:50.398 --> 19:54.109
It's hard adjusting to life here
when you've arrived from the city.

19:54.110 --> 19:57.278
One for regional PH docs,
one for us here, our public health center,

19:57.279 --> 19:59.572
Youth Association, Women's Association…

19:59.573 --> 20:01.658
Anyway, I'll invite you
to all the group chats.

20:01.659 --> 20:03.952
People live here
just like any other place.

20:03.953 --> 20:05.995
How different could it be?

20:05.996 --> 20:09.457
Stop making such a big fuss,
and take it slow with stuff like that.

20:09.458 --> 20:11.501
We haven't even shown him his office yet.

20:11.502 --> 20:13.712
Your office is that way.

20:13.713 --> 20:15.130
Exam room number one.

20:15.131 --> 20:17.173
We gave you the biggest room.

20:17.174 --> 20:20.218
Since you're a medical specialist.

20:20.219 --> 20:22.805
Here, this way. You should see your room.

20:25.349 --> 20:27.601
A mercury sphygmomanometer.
:cue

20:28.894 --> 20:31.105
It's a bit outdated, isn't it?

20:31.772 --> 20:35.317
We do bring it up every year,
but nothing ever changes.

20:35.901 --> 20:39.237
I know it's rather shoddy compared
to the university hospitals in Seoul,

20:39.238 --> 20:42.157
but I doubt you'll have any major issues.

20:42.158 --> 20:45.326
The patients who visit our center

20:45.327 --> 20:48.663
don't come here
because of anything bad in particular,

20:48.664 --> 20:50.457
but because of chronic illnesses.

20:50.458 --> 20:51.958
Blood pressure, diabetes, and arthritis.

20:51.959 --> 20:55.503
They just live with those conditions
their whole lives.

20:55.504 --> 20:58.716
One granny said she hurt everywhere
except her eyebrows.

20:59.800 --> 21:01.594
We should still get a new BP monitor.

21:04.096 --> 21:05.514
Right.

21:13.397 --> 21:15.899
You've seen
pretty much everything now.

21:15.900 --> 21:17.651
Should I get you something to drink?

21:18.235 --> 21:19.986
No, I just want to wash up right now.

21:19.987 --> 21:22.822
Uh. Here, your key.

21:22.823 --> 21:24.282
Right.

21:24.283 --> 21:28.286
To get to your room,
go up like this, go up like this,

21:28.287 --> 21:30.831
then go up like this,
and it's the first room on the left.

21:35.586 --> 21:37.087
Man, that's a lot better.

22:15.709 --> 22:16.918
What happened?

22:16.919 --> 22:18.545
There was a centipede this big!

22:18.546 --> 22:20.547
It fell on my face and…

22:20.548 --> 22:21.714
My goodness.

22:21.715 --> 22:24.259
And here I was thinking
it was something serious.

22:24.260 --> 22:26.386
I bet the centipede
was more startled than you.

22:26.387 --> 22:30.348
Centipedes aren't the only things here.
And they're tame compared to the rest.

22:30.349 --> 22:32.977
Snakes, house centipedes, spiders…

22:33.644 --> 22:36.396
Just think of them as your roommates.

22:36.397 --> 22:38.065
BUG SPRAY

23:14.894 --> 23:17.146
Oh. This isn't mine.

23:30.284 --> 23:31.285
No way.

23:32.328 --> 23:33.786
That woman with the bottle?

23:45.841 --> 23:47.342
What now?

23:47.343 --> 23:48.676
Another bug?

23:48.677 --> 23:49.761
No.

23:49.762 --> 23:52.805
I think my suitcase got swapped,
and I'm not sure what to do.

23:52.806 --> 23:54.724
It's one thing after another
with this guy.

23:54.725 --> 23:58.019
For that, you'll have to go
to the village hall.

23:58.020 --> 24:00.730
If you tell
the Youth Association members there,

24:00.731 --> 24:02.899
they'll help you out
with just about anything.

24:02.900 --> 24:03.983
Go there.

24:03.984 --> 24:06.152
The village hall? Okay. Thank you.
:cue

24:09.323 --> 24:10.324
Oh, man.

24:27.257 --> 24:30.135
Are you kidding me right now?

24:33.430 --> 24:35.724
What's a car like that
doing on an island like this?

24:36.225 --> 24:38.518
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

24:38.519 --> 24:40.396
- Thanks for your hard work.
- Sure.

24:41.230 --> 24:42.564
How did the home visit go?

24:43.315 --> 24:45.900
How was the granny doing?
Is she better now?

24:45.901 --> 24:47.236
Yes, she's better now.

24:49.363 --> 24:53.741
Ms. Hwang, what exactly
are the criteria for home visits?

24:53.742 --> 24:55.077
What do you mean by that?

24:55.661 --> 24:57.996
I just don't think it's fair
that even the patients

24:57.997 --> 25:00.248
who are perfectly capable
of getting around

25:00.249 --> 25:01.708
get to apply for home visits.

25:01.709 --> 25:02.876
Ah.

25:03.502 --> 25:06.587
Right, it can be unfair.

25:06.588 --> 25:08.673
But such are human affairs.

25:08.674 --> 25:11.634
Not everything can be
perfectly fair, you know?

25:11.635 --> 25:12.928
Yes.

25:14.430 --> 25:16.849
Then I'll be turning down home visits.

25:17.516 --> 25:18.599
What?

25:18.600 --> 25:21.937
To my understanding, PH docs
aren't obligated to perform home visits.

25:29.945 --> 25:32.196
Wow, that guy…

25:32.197 --> 25:34.450
PYEONDONGDO VILLAGE HALL

25:35.367 --> 25:39.287
So, your suitcase got mixed up
with someone else's on the ferry?

25:39.288 --> 25:41.497
Yes. I think it got mixed up
with some woman's.

25:41.498 --> 25:43.250
She had short hair.

25:44.793 --> 25:46.377
By the way,

25:46.378 --> 25:49.338
weren't there any accidents
involving one of the passengers?

25:49.339 --> 25:51.758
Like someone falling into the water or…

25:51.759 --> 25:54.427
We've never had accidents
involving passengers.

25:54.428 --> 25:57.931
Our ferry, the Hansol No. 3,
has been accident-free for 20 years.

25:59.850 --> 26:01.225
Hold on.

26:01.226 --> 26:04.188
It must have gotten mixed up
with Granny Mija's granddaughter's.

26:05.439 --> 26:06.773
Sorry? Granddaughter?

26:06.774 --> 26:10.319
Oh, my. You must really
not remember, Doctor.

26:11.361 --> 26:15.406
The one who carried you on her back
was Granny Mija's granddaughter.

26:15.407 --> 26:17.241
- Granddaughter?
- But anyway,

26:17.242 --> 26:19.660
if you're a doctor, why are you so feeble?

26:19.661 --> 26:22.371
Hey, quit it!

26:22.372 --> 26:24.123
That's how your suitcase got mixed up.

26:24.124 --> 26:26.835
So the one who carried me was a woman?

26:30.589 --> 26:33.425
I mean, all these houses
have red rooftops.

26:34.510 --> 26:36.929
Which red rooftop were they talking about?

26:39.681 --> 26:42.308
And what does "follow the road
and go straight" mean?

26:42.309 --> 26:44.018
I've been walking straight forever.

26:44.019 --> 26:46.522
Help!

26:47.523 --> 26:48.774
Move!

26:52.111 --> 26:53.694
Run!

26:56.448 --> 27:00.369
:cue

27:40.492 --> 27:42.953
- Hurry! This way!
- Run!

27:49.877 --> 27:52.129
No!

28:00.888 --> 28:03.598
Deokgu!

28:03.599 --> 28:05.975
Goodness me, where did you go?

28:05.976 --> 28:08.769
Oh, no, Deokgu!

28:08.770 --> 28:11.147
I'm sorry!

28:11.148 --> 28:13.149
I was wondering where you had run off to.

28:13.150 --> 28:15.234
- Come here. Gosh, I'm sorry.
- Deokgu?

28:15.235 --> 28:17.779
- Deokgu?
- Where have you been?

28:18.697 --> 28:20.239
Come here.

28:20.240 --> 28:21.324
You bad boy. Let's go.

28:21.325 --> 28:22.743
- Come on.
- Auntie!

28:24.036 --> 28:26.662
You're Hari, aren't you?

28:26.663 --> 28:31.500
-  Auntie! I'm so happy to see you!
- Oh, my!

28:31.501 --> 28:33.085
Have you been well?

28:33.086 --> 28:34.462
What are you doing here?

28:35.964 --> 28:38.299
Deokgu's grown so big. Hi, Deokgu.

28:38.300 --> 28:40.177
-  You're still cute.
- That's a friendly dog.

28:51.897 --> 28:53.607
Gosh, I'm sorry.

28:55.609 --> 28:58.612
I must have taken your suitcase
because I was so out of it.

28:59.279 --> 29:00.571
Check this one too.

29:00.572 --> 29:01.989
I'm sure it's mine.

29:01.990 --> 29:03.491
Well, you should still check.

29:03.492 --> 29:05.743
I opened it briefly.
The lock code was the same.

29:05.744 --> 29:08.580
Wow, then I guess
we must have the same birthday.

29:09.665 --> 29:11.248
November 6th?

29:11.249 --> 29:12.708
No, January 16th.

29:12.709 --> 29:14.127
I see.

29:28.308 --> 29:30.018
Oh, my. Why are these…

29:34.439 --> 29:36.607
MEDICAL PATCH
NARCOTIC PAINKILLERS

29:36.608 --> 29:38.275
CHAVOXIFEN
CHAVOXIFEN CITRATE

29:38.276 --> 29:39.653
"Chavoxifen"?

29:40.737 --> 29:43.699
That's a targeted agent.

29:54.084 --> 29:55.794
Looks like everything's here.

30:04.094 --> 30:05.803
- That's where it was.
- What's wrong?

30:05.804 --> 30:07.723
- Damn it.
- What?

30:09.141 --> 30:11.893
- Goodness, let me get that for you.
- Okay.

30:18.233 --> 30:19.901
Good.

30:21.028 --> 30:22.112
It's fine.

30:25.240 --> 30:26.699
All done.

30:26.700 --> 30:27.701
Right.

30:28.535 --> 30:31.413
Mine's good to go.
Shouldn't you check yours?

30:33.623 --> 30:34.750
Right.

30:53.685 --> 30:54.936
Oh, right.

30:56.688 --> 30:58.481
This also belongs to you, right?

30:58.482 --> 31:00.274
ELLMARP

31:00.275 --> 31:03.111
Thank you.
:cue

31:05.155 --> 31:06.823
Don't take that medication.

31:08.658 --> 31:10.910
I don't think it agrees with you.

31:10.911 --> 31:12.913
You were in serious danger
on the ferry earlier.

31:15.499 --> 31:16.500
Wait…

31:17.501 --> 31:20.920
Look who's talking about being in danger.

31:20.921 --> 31:22.379
What?

31:22.380 --> 31:24.256
What were you doing up there anyway?

31:24.257 --> 31:26.801
Were you trying to kill yourself?

31:26.802 --> 31:27.803
Me?

31:28.512 --> 31:29.595
Why on earth would I--

31:29.596 --> 31:32.099
I got into this whole mess
because I tried to save you.

31:32.682 --> 31:35.769
What the heck
are you talking about?

31:41.149 --> 31:43.609
Ms. Mija, it's so pretty out here!

31:43.610 --> 31:45.194
Check out the ocean.

31:45.195 --> 31:49.490
Goodness, what beauty is there
in something I see every day?

31:49.491 --> 31:52.993
To me, you're the prettiest thing
in the world, Hari.

31:52.994 --> 31:56.997
Hey, I take after my grandma.
Of course I'm pretty.

31:59.084 --> 32:00.460
Grandma, have you eaten yet?

32:04.673 --> 32:06.966
My cardigan went flying.

32:06.967 --> 32:09.845
-  I'll just have to get a new one.
- Hey, don't!

32:11.930 --> 32:14.598
No, don't!

32:14.599 --> 32:15.683
What?

32:15.684 --> 32:18.853
- Don't go.
- Oh, no. You have to be careful.

32:18.854 --> 32:20.312
It's dangerous up there!

32:20.313 --> 32:22.565
- Over here!
- What?

32:22.566 --> 32:25.277
I need help over here!

32:26.278 --> 32:27.444
Someone…

32:27.445 --> 32:29.613
Someone's fallen into the water!

32:29.614 --> 32:32.199
I think we have to stop the boat!

32:32.200 --> 32:33.909
What did you say?

32:33.910 --> 32:36.829
- I'll… I'll save her.
-  Careful!

32:36.830 --> 32:38.874
- I'll save you!
- Who are you trying to save?

32:40.208 --> 32:42.585
Oh, no. What do I do?

32:42.586 --> 32:44.670
- I'll save you!
- Wait!

32:44.671 --> 32:46.923
-  No… Damn it.
- Just hold on!

33:09.696 --> 33:10.905
I did that?

33:13.408 --> 33:16.912
I shouldn't have
knocked him out like that.

33:17.579 --> 33:20.123
Gosh, he's so freaking heavy.

33:21.833 --> 33:25.252
Excuse me, please wake up.

33:25.253 --> 33:27.380
You really don't remember anything?

33:29.966 --> 33:32.302
I don't remember that at all. I don't.

33:36.264 --> 33:37.890
Are you better now?

33:37.891 --> 33:39.517
Gosh. I'm totally…

33:41.811 --> 33:43.480
- Are you leaving?
- Of course!

33:45.398 --> 33:46.399
Take care!

33:49.444 --> 33:50.445
Oh, no.

33:58.536 --> 33:59.871
What's with that guy?

34:05.710 --> 34:08.045
:cue

34:08.046 --> 34:10.214
-  Yeah, on that side.
-  Yes.

34:10.215 --> 34:11.715
Did you return his suitcase?

34:11.716 --> 34:12.717
Yeah.

34:13.718 --> 34:15.761
And he didn't say anything weird?

34:15.762 --> 34:18.222
Sounded like he wasn't normal.

34:18.223 --> 34:19.640
Yeah, he's a total weirdo.

34:19.641 --> 34:22.810
You said you were going back
to the mainland again tomorrow.

34:22.811 --> 34:25.187
Why did you have to move your bags today

34:25.188 --> 34:27.273
and get mixed up with a guy like that?

34:27.274 --> 34:30.150
Tomorrow will come
with tomorrow's share of baggage.

34:30.151 --> 34:33.654
Why did you even come
all the way back to this island?

34:33.655 --> 34:35.906
Let's hurry. Mom and Dad must be hungry.

34:35.907 --> 34:38.701
Look at you. Fine, let's do that.

34:38.702 --> 34:39.703
Here we go.

34:42.914 --> 34:43.915
What the heck?

34:45.292 --> 34:47.002
Why's this thing open?

34:49.504 --> 34:52.006
No idea. I wonder why it was open.

34:52.007 --> 34:53.967
You drank from it, didn't you?

34:56.136 --> 34:58.762
I only did it because I was thirsty.

34:58.763 --> 35:02.349
Goodness me. Who did you get that from?

35:02.350 --> 35:04.393
I got it all from you, Granny.

35:04.394 --> 35:06.437
How are you so cute?

35:06.438 --> 35:08.355
I also got that all from you, Granny.

35:08.356 --> 35:10.275
My, my, you precious thing.

35:16.489 --> 35:19.367
Making up stories
just because I don't remember.

35:21.453 --> 35:23.996
Does she not realize
I ended up like that because of her?

35:23.997 --> 35:25.248
Man, this is just…

35:28.835 --> 35:31.795
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

35:35.008 --> 35:36.009
What the…

35:36.885 --> 35:39.429
What's this car doing here?

35:53.109 --> 35:54.110
BATHROOM

36:16.424 --> 36:19.719
I'm sorry. I thought
there was no one in here…

36:21.471 --> 36:23.348
You're the doctor who came today, right?

36:24.557 --> 36:26.559
Yes. I'm Do Jiui.

36:28.812 --> 36:29.938
I'm Hyeon Chiyeon.

36:34.526 --> 36:36.027
I heard you were carried here.

36:39.489 --> 36:40.824
I don't recall that.

36:42.659 --> 36:45.620
That's a relief.
I look forward to working with you.

36:51.000 --> 36:52.168
What the heck was that?

37:24.534 --> 37:25.535
Doctor.

37:27.287 --> 37:28.537
Aren't you hungry?

37:28.538 --> 37:31.291
You should treat us all
since it's your first day here.
:cue

37:33.168 --> 37:34.376
- Me?
- Yes.

37:34.377 --> 37:36.880
Dr. Chiyeon is waiting for you,
so hurry and come outside.

37:40.341 --> 37:41.843
Why should I be treating them?

37:42.552 --> 37:45.679
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT
BEST RESTAURANT IN PYEONDONGDO

37:45.680 --> 37:46.848
Hello.

37:48.558 --> 37:50.684
Auntie, we're here!

37:50.685 --> 37:52.145
Oh, you're here?

37:53.688 --> 37:55.482
It's so hot.

37:58.067 --> 37:59.777
- Oh, my.
- Huh?

37:59.778 --> 38:01.196
It's you again.

38:01.905 --> 38:04.531
- That was quite startling, wasn't it?
- Yes.

38:04.532 --> 38:06.658
- You two have already met?
- Yes.

38:06.659 --> 38:09.412
-  There was a minor incident.
- Ah.

38:09.996 --> 38:13.040
Auntie, we'll have the dish
that got rave reviews on that TV show.

38:13.041 --> 38:15.459
- The one we ordered in advance, please.
- Of course.

38:15.460 --> 38:17.045
- Just give me a moment.
-  Okay.

38:19.464 --> 38:21.299
What do you specialize in, Doctor?

38:22.217 --> 38:25.010
- Plastic surgery.
- Wow.

38:25.011 --> 38:28.305
You must have done very well in school.
Plastic surgery is so popular.

38:28.306 --> 38:29.389
Yes, well…

38:29.390 --> 38:32.142
You haven't chosen
your specialty yet, right?

38:32.143 --> 38:33.977
- That's right.
- Hmm.

38:33.978 --> 38:35.521
How about a plastic surgery clinic?

38:35.522 --> 38:38.774
If you opened a clinic in Gangnam,
I bet people would line up asking you

38:38.775 --> 38:41.069
to fix them up
to look like you.

38:42.320 --> 38:43.695
Hmm.

38:43.696 --> 38:45.280
I don't know.

38:45.281 --> 38:47.659
I'm not a huge fan of plastic surgeons.

38:48.243 --> 38:50.036
They just come across as money-grubbers.

38:51.538 --> 38:52.539
What did you say?

38:53.748 --> 38:55.834
Ah. I sure am hungry.

38:57.377 --> 38:59.086
Right to my face? Really?

38:59.087 --> 39:02.966
Here it comes, our signature dish.

39:04.384 --> 39:06.135
- Here you are.
-  Wow.

39:22.360 --> 39:23.945
- Uh…
- It looks so good.

39:28.324 --> 39:29.951
Thank you.

39:32.287 --> 39:34.246
And here's one for you, Doctor.

39:34.247 --> 39:35.831
Hurry up and eat.

39:35.832 --> 39:37.917
This is the only restaurant
in Pyeondongdo.

39:38.543 --> 39:42.088
If you don't hype it up,
you'll starve to death.

39:44.007 --> 39:45.550
There you go.

39:46.551 --> 39:49.220
- Yes, thank you.
-  Enjoy.

39:51.723 --> 39:53.933
-  Here.
-  Thank you.

39:54.684 --> 39:59.105
I don't know
if it'll suit your taste, Doctor.

40:00.189 --> 40:01.273
Hurry.

40:01.274 --> 40:04.485
Your only source of sustenance
for a whole year rests on it.

40:14.370 --> 40:15.746
Eat up.

40:26.841 --> 40:29.426
Eh?

40:38.645 --> 40:40.896
Yes, this is Cliffside.

40:40.897 --> 40:41.898
Yes.

40:42.565 --> 40:43.566
What?

40:44.067 --> 40:45.859
They're all here.

40:45.860 --> 40:46.861
Okay.

40:47.695 --> 40:50.781
The chief is asking for one doctor
back at the center…

40:50.782 --> 40:52.491
- I'll go.
-  What?

40:52.492 --> 40:54.159
But it's your first day.

40:54.160 --> 40:56.913
What can I say? I'm a workaholic.
I'll finish it when I get back.
:cue

41:07.799 --> 41:09.384
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

41:10.969 --> 41:12.177
Mr. Park.

41:12.178 --> 41:13.261
CLOSED

41:13.262 --> 41:14.596
Ah!

41:14.597 --> 41:18.141
Oh, Doctor. Did you find your suitcase?

41:18.142 --> 41:21.478
Yes, thanks to you.
But can you tell me how you're sick?

41:21.479 --> 41:26.608
I think I have indigestion.
My chest is really stuffy.

41:26.609 --> 41:28.778
So, give me some Umetazole.

41:29.404 --> 41:31.239
- Umetazole?
- Ah.

41:31.739 --> 41:33.615
I think I have a bad case of indigestion.

41:33.616 --> 41:36.536
So bad that I threw up
everything I ate for breakfast.

41:37.161 --> 41:40.414
I have fishing customers coming,
so I have to get going right away.

41:40.415 --> 41:42.000
Please hurry and give it to me.

41:42.667 --> 41:45.127
Let's get inside
so I can take a look at you first.

41:45.128 --> 41:46.879
- Let's take this inside.
- Okay.

41:50.133 --> 41:52.300
Here.

41:52.301 --> 41:53.802
The left side.

41:53.803 --> 41:55.887
My left arm's also really sore.

41:55.888 --> 41:57.597
It's killing me.

41:57.598 --> 41:59.850
Does it feel as if someone's wringing it?

41:59.851 --> 42:02.270
Yes. It does kind of feel like that.

42:02.979 --> 42:06.064
I must have serious indigestion.

42:06.065 --> 42:09.484
Just give me Umetazole.
I'll be fine once I take it.

42:09.485 --> 42:11.946
- I've always taken it.
- Let me take your blood pressure.

42:13.489 --> 42:15.115
Hey, now.

42:15.116 --> 42:18.118
I have indigestion.
Why even bother taking my blood pressure?

42:42.518 --> 42:45.271
Stuffiness in his left chest,
trouble breathing,

42:45.855 --> 42:49.316
chest pains that feel as though
someone's wringing his chest,

42:49.317 --> 42:54.447
high blood pressure, nausea,
and even referred pain in the left arm.

42:55.698 --> 42:57.157
All signs point to an MI.

42:57.158 --> 42:59.702
MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION

43:06.417 --> 43:08.127
Wait here for a moment.

43:08.878 --> 43:09.879
Okay.

43:27.897 --> 43:28.898
UMETAZOLE

43:33.277 --> 43:35.655
- Can you try taking this?
- Huh?

43:36.864 --> 43:38.950
Put it under your tongue,
and let it melt.

43:40.076 --> 43:41.077
Okay.

44:09.188 --> 44:10.189
What the…

44:11.149 --> 44:12.942
I feel better already.

44:13.568 --> 44:15.402
He wasn't supposed to feel better.

44:15.403 --> 44:18.739
The fact that the NTG worked
within minutes means

44:19.323 --> 44:22.701
there's a higher than 80% chance that
we're looking at a myocardial infarction.
:cue

44:22.702 --> 44:25.370
PATIENT RECORD QUERY
MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION, NTG

44:25.371 --> 44:29.166
I thought you were a weakling
because a girl carried you here,

44:29.167 --> 44:31.376
but you're an amazing doctor.

44:31.377 --> 44:34.004
Pyeondongdo has nothing
to worry about now.

44:34.005 --> 44:38.509
If anything troubles you during your stay,
feel free to tell me about it.

44:39.260 --> 44:42.095
Now, I've got urgent business
to attend to, so I'll--

44:42.096 --> 44:44.097
No, you shouldn't leave right now.

44:44.098 --> 44:45.557
Why?

44:45.558 --> 44:47.350
That wasn't digestive medicine.

44:47.351 --> 44:49.353
It was a drug
for myocardial infarction patients.

44:50.188 --> 44:52.230
The fact that your condition improved

44:52.231 --> 44:55.650
means there's a higher than 80% chance
of you getting a heart attack.

44:55.651 --> 44:57.402
We have to get you to a big hospital.

44:57.403 --> 45:01.573
Oh, come on.
I see our new doctor's a total worrywart.

45:01.574 --> 45:04.159
A big hospital? Please, I'll be fine!

45:04.160 --> 45:06.286
I'm telling you, you have to go right now!

45:06.287 --> 45:09.039
Don't worry. I know my body best.

45:09.040 --> 45:10.165
Mr. Park!

45:10.166 --> 45:11.583
Move aside!

45:11.584 --> 45:14.628
If I get hit with a fee for bailing,
will you take responsibility?

45:14.629 --> 45:16.922
Keep this up
and something bad will happen to you.

45:16.923 --> 45:18.340
Geez.

45:18.341 --> 45:22.427
Doctor, you said there was an 80% chance
of me getting a heart attack, right?

45:22.428 --> 45:25.223
But there's a 100% chance
of my fishing customers coming!

45:26.390 --> 45:27.849
Fine.

45:27.850 --> 45:31.311
I'll just give my customers a ride,
then go to a hospital, so move.

45:31.312 --> 45:32.854
You could end up passing away.

45:32.855 --> 45:34.065
What do you mean, pass…

45:39.820 --> 45:40.821
What now?

45:42.073 --> 45:43.074
Pass away?

45:43.783 --> 45:44.825
Yes.

45:48.037 --> 45:50.414
That's no good.

45:51.624 --> 45:52.625
What am I to do?

45:53.626 --> 45:54.627
So…

45:55.169 --> 45:57.213
You're saying I have to go no matter what?

46:03.052 --> 46:04.636
Okay.

46:04.637 --> 46:06.596
I should listen to you.

46:06.597 --> 46:09.349
Take a seat outside,
and I'll get right back to you.

46:09.350 --> 46:11.978
I guess I'll do that.

46:26.701 --> 46:28.868
Yes, Ms. Hwang.
We have an emergency patient.

46:28.869 --> 46:30.913
He's a myocardial infarction patient.
I'll…

46:31.497 --> 46:33.040
What? A chopper?

46:35.001 --> 46:36.585
Mr. Park, they're sending a chopper…

46:40.214 --> 46:41.215
Mr. Park?

46:47.430 --> 46:48.431
Mr. Park?

46:52.977 --> 46:54.312
Damn it.

46:54.979 --> 46:57.481
Trust me, I know my own body best.

47:00.901 --> 47:03.404
Goodness, I'm going to miss my customers.

47:06.365 --> 47:10.243
What do you mean
the patient's gone missing?

47:10.244 --> 47:12.495
He slipped out
while I was on the phone with you…

47:12.496 --> 47:14.706
What about the chopper?

47:14.707 --> 47:17.834
If we call one with no patient,
our center will be penalized.

47:17.835 --> 47:19.127
He'll get on that chopper.

47:19.128 --> 47:23.340
Given his response to NTG,
he may end up having a heart attack.

47:23.341 --> 47:25.426
So let's find him as quickly as we can.

47:26.010 --> 47:27.927
Is he not picking up his phone?

47:27.928 --> 47:29.930
Why isn't he answering his phone?

47:31.390 --> 47:33.558
-  The fishing boat.
- What?

47:33.559 --> 47:35.310
He said he had fishing customers.

47:35.311 --> 47:36.562
- Let's go!
- Let's hurry.

47:37.813 --> 47:39.023
Mr. Park!

47:39.899 --> 47:42.068
Mr. Park!

47:43.903 --> 47:44.986
Mr. Park!
:cue

47:44.987 --> 47:46.030
Mr. Park!

47:48.949 --> 47:52.118
- Mr. Park!
- Mr. Park. Are you okay?

47:52.119 --> 47:53.828
You have to come with us right now.

47:53.829 --> 47:55.580
What brings you all here?

47:55.581 --> 47:57.499
Doesn't your body feel kind of iffy?

47:57.500 --> 48:01.419
Why the hell did you all follow me here?
I told you I'm fine, didn't I?

48:01.420 --> 48:03.380
I know my body best!

48:03.381 --> 48:06.216
- But still, you should…
- Mr. Park, that's all temporary.

48:06.217 --> 48:07.509
- You--
- I've heard enough.

48:07.510 --> 48:10.387
Just go about your business. I said, go!

48:10.388 --> 48:12.430
- I'm hella busy, okay?
- Okay.

48:12.431 --> 48:14.015
Then just a quick check.

48:14.016 --> 48:17.143
I'm fine! Just go.

48:17.144 --> 48:19.229
Hello, sir, come this way.

48:19.230 --> 48:20.855
This way. Get on the boat.

48:20.856 --> 48:23.733
- I said go away.
- Okay.

48:23.734 --> 48:25.151
I'm fine!

48:25.152 --> 48:26.861
- Okay.
- Here, get in.

48:26.862 --> 48:28.280
- This one, right?
- Yes.

48:29.240 --> 48:31.408
Scram! Stop blocking the way!

48:31.409 --> 48:32.784
Gosh, we're leaving.

48:32.785 --> 48:35.496
Geez, I told them I was fine.

48:40.084 --> 48:44.337
Gosh, those sudden outbursts
must be what's keeping him so feisty.

48:48.551 --> 48:51.010
- Mr. Park!
- Oh, no! Mr. Park!

48:51.011 --> 48:53.680
Mr. Park! Oh heavens, what do we do?

48:53.681 --> 48:55.640
Goodness, Mr. Park.

48:55.641 --> 48:57.143
I'll administer CPR.

48:57.977 --> 48:59.519
- Please measure the time.
- Oh, no.

48:59.520 --> 49:00.521
Right.

49:06.110 --> 49:08.696
Yes, this is Pyeondongdo.

49:09.655 --> 49:11.323
The chopper will be arriving soon.

49:12.408 --> 49:14.827
Goodness, Mr. Park.

49:29.800 --> 49:31.844
MEDICAL HELICOPTER

49:49.236 --> 49:52.155
The patient is a 65-year-old man.
He came in about 30 minutes ago,

49:52.156 --> 49:54.866
thinking it was indigestion,
complaining of chest pain.

49:54.867 --> 49:58.745
I administered NTG. He refused to visit
a hospital and collapsed within an hour.

49:58.746 --> 50:01.748
He was in a state of stupor
with no pulse, so I administered CPR.

50:01.749 --> 50:04.209
And we got ROSC within five minutes.

50:04.210 --> 50:05.877
Are you a doctor?

50:05.878 --> 50:07.588
Sorry? Oh, yes.

50:08.172 --> 50:10.507
Then come with us. Get in.

50:10.508 --> 50:12.258
- Come on.
- Go.

50:12.259 --> 50:14.553
- Go!
- We should hurry! We'll be late!

51:02.434 --> 51:04.645
ASONG HOSPITAL
:cue

51:09.149 --> 51:12.277
Ventricular wall motion is poor.
We'll have to do an emergency CAG.

51:12.278 --> 51:13.361
Yes, understood.

51:13.362 --> 51:14.946
CORONARY ANGIOGRAPHY

51:14.947 --> 51:17.449
RESTRICTED AREA

51:20.411 --> 51:21.953
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

51:23.747 --> 51:26.291
- Thank you for a job well done.
- Thank you.

51:26.292 --> 51:27.293
Take care.

51:28.127 --> 51:30.296
- Sir, just a moment.
- Yes?

51:31.338 --> 51:33.172
- What about me?
- Huh?

51:33.173 --> 51:34.340
- Huh?
- What do you mean?

51:34.341 --> 51:36.050
How do I get back?

51:36.051 --> 51:38.344
You? Why are you asking me that?

51:38.345 --> 51:40.306
I guess you could ask your health center.

51:40.848 --> 51:42.223
I'm leaving now.

51:42.224 --> 51:43.516
- Bye.
- Okay.

51:43.517 --> 51:44.977
Safe travels.

51:46.312 --> 51:49.314
Yes, situation room.
Yeopoong One has finished transferring…

51:49.315 --> 51:52.735
So we're just supposed to
find our own way back home, huh?

51:55.070 --> 51:57.281
Then why the hell
did he tell me to come? Damn it.

52:00.117 --> 52:01.535
How am I supposed to get back?

52:02.202 --> 52:06.956
The last ferry's already gone
for the day, so find a motel, sleep there,

52:06.957 --> 52:09.459
and take the first ferry back tomorrow.

52:09.460 --> 52:10.710
Oh, a ferry?

52:10.711 --> 52:13.129
Of course, a ferry.
What else would you take? A train?

52:13.130 --> 52:14.882
Never mind. Yes, I understand.

52:15.382 --> 52:16.716
Good work today.

52:19.386 --> 52:20.387
That's it?

52:22.473 --> 52:23.474
Oh, come on.

52:28.395 --> 52:29.396
Man, I'm so exhausted.

52:31.023 --> 52:32.024
I'm starving.

52:46.080 --> 52:48.999
Man, to think this is
my first meal in 24 hours…

53:11.855 --> 53:14.357
Clap, clap, clap, welcome to hell.

53:14.358 --> 53:15.775
You won a ticket to hell!

53:15.776 --> 53:17.777
Pyeondongdo of all places?

53:17.778 --> 53:20.238
Hang on for a year,
then make a run for the mainland.

53:20.239 --> 53:22.699
If you just got here,
does that mean you have 340 days

53:22.700 --> 53:25.785
until you're allowed to transfer
to a different province?

53:25.786 --> 53:28.413
"If you just got here,
does that mean you have 340 days?"

53:28.414 --> 53:29.956
Is this guy mocking me right now?

53:29.957 --> 53:32.792
It's because you were
a traitor to the nation in your past life.

53:32.793 --> 53:36.003
I was a helmsman on the turtle ship!
So why'd I get sent to an island?

53:36.004 --> 53:39.799
Come on, 340 days will go by
in the blink of an eye.

53:39.800 --> 53:42.260
The only downside is that
you don't get to go on leave.

53:42.261 --> 53:45.055
Man, these people are making me
lose my appetite.

54:06.577 --> 54:09.662
I'm so tired…

54:15.711 --> 54:18.338
I should eat before I sleep.
I'm really hungry…

54:20.340 --> 54:22.259
That ramyeon is going to taste so good.

54:43.655 --> 54:45.407
Hello?

54:46.074 --> 54:47.784
Doctor, why aren't you here yet?

54:50.704 --> 54:52.038
I'm still at the…

54:52.039 --> 54:53.956
Why are you still on the mainland?

54:53.957 --> 54:56.083
You should've taken the first ferry back!

54:56.084 --> 55:00.421
Do you have any idea how busy it gets
at a public health center?

55:00.422 --> 55:02.507
It's because of the emergency--

55:02.508 --> 55:04.759
That was yesterday, not today!

55:04.760 --> 55:07.094
Hurry back
or you'll be reported for desertion.

55:07.095 --> 55:08.888
One warning for abandoning your post.

55:08.889 --> 55:10.097
Two warnings

55:10.098 --> 55:12.808
and you're barred
from transferring provinces.

55:12.809 --> 55:14.977
You wanna get tied down here
for three years, huh?

55:14.978 --> 55:18.941
I'm going!
I'll get going right now.

55:19.775 --> 55:22.194
Oh, for crying out loud.
:cue

55:36.250 --> 55:39.461
YEOPOONG MARINE TRANSPORT

55:42.714 --> 55:43.715
Ah.

55:53.809 --> 55:56.060
You told me that I could ask you for help

55:56.061 --> 55:59.815
if I was having any trouble
with something.

56:00.315 --> 56:01.983
It's about Pyeondongdo.

56:01.984 --> 56:04.819
Is there any other way to get there
that's not by ferry?

56:04.820 --> 56:07.363
I'd be okay with
a chopper or something too.

56:07.364 --> 56:10.366
Stop talking nonsense
and get your tail over here.

56:10.367 --> 56:12.952
And from now on,
if you're having trouble with anything,

56:12.953 --> 56:15.496
don't tell me about it
and just take care of it yourself.

56:15.497 --> 56:17.081
- I'm hanging up now!
- Hold on.

56:17.082 --> 56:18.500
Hello? Ms. Hwang…

56:19.918 --> 56:21.335
Are you kidding me?

56:21.336 --> 56:24.088
The ship bound for Pyeondongdo

56:24.089 --> 56:25.507
is now departing.

56:26.675 --> 56:30.971
All remaining passengers,
please board the ship at this time.

57:30.280 --> 57:32.282
:cue

58:04.147 --> 58:08.568
The three things one must avoid
encountering on an island.

58:12.906 --> 58:15.366
- Incidents…
- Please wake up.

58:15.367 --> 58:16.827
Move!

58:23.834 --> 58:24.835
People…

58:32.843 --> 58:34.094
All done.

58:39.474 --> 58:40.475
And…

59:20.766 --> 59:25.144
THE THREE THINGS ONE MUST AVOID
ENCOUNTERING ON AN ISLAND

59:25.145 --> 59:27.146
INCIDENTS,

59:27.147 --> 59:29.648
PEOPLE,

59:29.649 --> 59:32.194
AND…

59:45.290 --> 59:48.210
"SUN, PLEASE COME OUT
OF THE CLOUDS"

01:00:00.305 --> 01:00:03.307
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:00:03.308 --> 01:00:05.768
I mean, why do we keep
running into each other?

01:00:05.769 --> 01:00:07.978
Just be on your way
and stop crossing the line.

01:00:07.979 --> 01:00:09.730
Look at me. I almost crossed the line.

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:11.191
Hey!

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:14.736
Do you really not remember me?

01:00:16.112 --> 01:00:18.781
He actually went to
the county office to file a complaint.

01:00:18.782 --> 01:00:20.784
Come over here
if you've got a death wish.

01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:23.911
Why get the surgery
if you're going to act like this?

01:00:23.912 --> 01:00:26.455
I'm scared! Come on.

01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:28.041
Are we expecting someone?

01:00:33.547 --> 01:00:35.549
Subtitle translation by: Yoon Hyuk Park
